  "title": "Shortest delivery round",
  "kind": "code",
  "language": "go",
  "level": 5,
  "statement": "A courier starts at stop 1, must visit every other stop exactly once, and then return to stop 1. Travel times are given as a matrix: d[i][j] is the time to go from stop i to stop j. The matrix is not necessarily symmetric (d[i][j] can differ from d[j][i]) and does not necessarily satisfy the triangle inequality. Print the smallest total travel time of such a round.\n\nInput: the first line holds n (1 <= n <= 16). Each of the next n lines holds n integers: line i holds d[i][1] .. d[i][n] (0 <= d[i][j] <= 1000000, d[i][i] = 0).\n\nOutput: one line with the minimum total time. With n = 1 the courier does not move and the answer is 0. Trying every order (15! of them) is far too slow for n = 16.\n\nExample\nInput:\n4\n0 10 15 20\n5 0 9 10\n6 13 0 12\n8 8 9 0\nOutput:\n35\n(1 -> 2 -> 4 -> 3 -> 1 takes 10 + 10 + 9 + 6 = 35.)",
  "starter_code": "package main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\treader := bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)\n\tvar n int\n\tfmt.Fscan(reader, &n)\n\td := make([][]int, n)\n\tfor i := range d {\n\t\td[i] = make([]int, n)\n\t\tfor j := range d[i] {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fscan(reader, &d[i][j])\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// Print the shortest round that starts and ends at stop 1\n}\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 2000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
  "timer_seconds": 1800,
